{number: 173}
{title: No One Ever Cared for Me Like Jesus}
{key: Eb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
I would [Eb] love to tell you what I think of Jesus,
Since I [Bb7] found in Him a friend so strong and [Eb] true;
I would tell you how He changed my life completely;
He did [Bb7] something no other friend could [Eb] do.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
No [Ab] one ever cared for me like [Eb] Jesus;
There's no [Bb7] other friend so kind as [Eb] He;
No [Ab] one else could take the sin and darkness [Eb] from me;
O how [Bb7] much He cared for [Eb] me!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
All my [Eb] life was full of sin when Jesus found me;
All my [Bb7] heart was full of misery and [Eb] woe,
Jesus placed His strong arms about me
And He [Bb7] led me in the way I ought to [Eb] go.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Ev'ry [Eb] day He comes to me with new assurance;
More and [Bb7] more I understand His word of [Eb] love.
But I'll never know just why He came to save me,
Till someday I [Bb7] see His blessed face a-[Eb] bove.
{end_of_verse}
